<?xml version="1.0"?>
<body language="English">
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00000" index="0">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ecruteak used to have two towers, one\neast and one west.\rNow it’s one tower and a crispy one.\nInsurance ain’t cover it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00001" index="1">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They talkin’ about rebuildin’ the Burned\nTower? Two towers again!\rThey been sayin’ that since ’87.\nCity contract. You know how it go.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00002" index="2">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Hmm... I think I just heard a woman\nscreamin’...\rIs that just me? It’s always just me.\nMy doctor say it’s “stress.”</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00003" index="3">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The Dancers ALWAYS rehearsin’ at the\nDance Theater.\rI watched for six hours. I’m not a\ncreep. I’m a fan. There’s a difference.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00004" index="4">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">I’m finna rehearse at the Dance\nTheater. Wanna come? I do interpretive\fdance.\fI interpret bills I can’t pay.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00005" index="5">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The tower that used to be here...\nIt was WAY taller before it burned.\rNow it’s a fixer-upper. Big time.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00006" index="6">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Three big homies ran off in three\ndifferent directions!\rWhat WAS that?! Like a family reunion\nwhen the check come.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00007" index="7">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">They gon’ start rebuildin’ this tower\nSOON! Any year now. Any decade.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00008" index="8">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Oh! That’s a nice homie you walkin’\nwith! They lift you up, don’t they?\rLike a light in the dark.\rSpeakin’ of lights, the Lighthouse homie\nin Olivine got sick.\fNow the boats crashin’. Shipping\fdelayed. My package LATE.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00009" index="9">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The Lighthouse homie in Olivine all\nbetter!\rBoats sailin’ at night again.\nMy package FINALLY came. It’s socks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00010" index="10">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Go west from this city and you\nhit a port called Olivine City.\rWhen your homie learn Hydrant Wave,\nyou can hit the ocean from\fRoute 40 without no boat!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00011" index="11">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ecruteak City\nOld Town. Older Heads.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00012" index="12">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ecruteak City Block\nBoss: Morty\fSees the Future. Still Late Though.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00013" index="13">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ecruteak Dance Theater\nNo Twerking</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00014" index="14">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Burned Tower\nDestroyed by a mysterious fire.\rStay away, it’s unsafe.\nWe mean it this time.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00015" index="15">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Barrier Station to Bell Tower\nNo Trespassin’ for the Unworthy</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00016" index="16">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">{SIZE 200}BONK!!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00017" index="17">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">{STRVAR_1 3, 1, 0}: How...? How is this\npossible? How I lose to\fsome DANCERS...?\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00018" index="18">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">{STRVAR_1 3, 1, 0}: You was watchin’ me,\n{STRVAR_1 3, 0, 0}...\rYeah, that’s right!\rI never thought beatin’ five\nDancers would be this hard...\rThey beat me into the ground...\r...\rYou here for the same reason,\nright?\rDon’t get cocky just ’cause you\nbeat The Feds!\rThese Dancers is CRAZY strong.\rGo ahead! See if you can beat ’em.\rBut I ain’t goin’ back in there.\nI don’t wanna watch you win.\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0612_T27_00019" index="19">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Way back in the day...\rWhen this tower burned down,\nthree nameless homies died in it.\rThen a rainbow-colored homie\ncame down from the sky and\fsomehow brought ’em back...\rPeople got scared of power like\nwhat that rainbow homie showed.\rThey tried to control it by force.\rThe nameless homies ain’t\nfight back. Instead, they was\fso sad they just left.\rThe Ecruteak Block Boss been\npassin’ down this legend. Me?\rI was a Hustler way back when.\nHo ho ho!</language>
	</row>
</body>
